coder › Done — implemented and committed on work/main as `f5234d1`.

**What changed**
- `src/limiter.ts`: added private `tokens` and `last` state, a private `refill()` that clamps backwards elapsed time to 0 and refills `elapsed / 1000 * refillPerSecond` capped at `capacity`; `tryTake(n = 1)` refuses `n > capacity` up front, then refills and only subtracts when `tokens >= n`; `get available` refills and returns the (possibly fractional) token count.
- `src/limiter.test.ts`: kept the existing "starts full" test and added six injected-`now` tests covering drain, no-take-on-failure, fractional refill (0.5 at 500 ms), capping at capacity, refusing `n > capacity` when full, and continuous refill between takes — 7 tests total.

**One decision the plan didn't state**: the plan said to initialise `tokens`/`last` as field initializers (`private tokens = this.capacity`), but under bun's transpiler class-field initializers run before parameter-property assignments, so `this.now`/`this.capacity` were still undefined at that point (first run failed with `TypeError: this.now is not a function`). I kept the readonly parameter-property constructor shape and instead declared the private fields and assigned them in the constructor body, which runs after parameter properties are bound. Everything else follows the spec exactly.

